# systemd unit ExecStart can pin a dev _build path — dune clean turns it into an infinite restart loop

## Steps to Reproduce

1. TODO: Add steps

## Expected Behavior

TODO: Describe expected behavior

## Actual Behavior

TODO: Describe actual behavior

## Symptom

c2c_binary_for_unit (c2c_relay_systemd.ml:194-203) falls back to argv[0] when the canonical install path is absent - running from a checkout bakes a dev _build binary path into a boot unit with Restart=always and StartLimitIntervalSec=0. A dune clean, worktree removal, or prefix change (without re-running install self or relay enable, which do rewrite the unit) leaves a permanently failing unit retrying every 5s forever; the in-supervisor binary-change detection re-execs self and never notices the unit ExecStart went stale.

## Fix direction

Refuse to embed a _build path (require an installed binary or an explicit override flag), or add a path-existence guard plus a doctor check.

## Evidence

CLI review 2026-09-17.